# __PROJECT_NAME__

A modular Flaxon JSON API. No database, admin or frontend tooling: just routes,
validation, OpenAPI docs and tests.

```bash
python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
cp .env.example .env        # local development settings
python -m flaxon run app:app --reload
python -m pytest
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs for the interactive API docs.

- `app.py`: app factory; mounts modules and applies trusted-host protection.
- `settings.py`: configuration read from the environment (`.env` is optional).
- `modules/items/module.py`: a sample feature. Copy it for each new feature.
- `tests/`: runs through Flaxon's `TestClient`; no server needed.

Items are stored in memory and reset on restart. For a database with migrations,
create a project with `flaxon new <name> --template api-db`.

Before deploying, set `FLAXON_ALLOWED_HOSTS` to your real hostnames.

[Documentation](https://flaxon-website.vercel.app/docs.html)
